<h3> MINIBIOGRAPHY OF WANGARI MAATHAI</h3>
<body>
<p>Wangari Maaathai was a kenyan environmentalist, political activist and founder of the green belt movement.<br> She was born on April 1,1940 in Nyeri ,Kenya . Wangari became famous for encouraging women to plant trees to protect the environment and to improve their livelihoods.<br> In 2004, she become the <b>the 1<sup>st</sup> African woman</b> to receive the<b> nobel prize</b> for her contribution to suistainable development democracy and peace. <br> She is rememberd as a strong leader who fought for environmental conservation and human rights. </p>

